# Game Architecture

- Physics is pure: `tick(state, inputs) → newState` with no side effects or DOM access
- `GameEngine` owns the rAF loop lifecycle; components subscribe via hooks only
- Collision uses AABB; ball angle varies by hit offset from paddle center
- Win condition is checked inside `tick`; engine transitions to `gameover` status
- Serve countdown and pause are engine responsibilities, not physics
- Reset and start flow goes through `GameEngine`, not React state inside the loop

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — pure tick
export function tick(state: GameState, inputs: Inputs): GameState { ... }

// ❌ BAD — physics coupled to canvas
export function tick(ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D, ...) { ... }
```
